WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:03.899
Film Courage: How do we know our own writing
level, the level that we’re at.

00:00:03.899 --> 00:00:08.010
We all think that we’re good at something
or excellent at something.

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:12.200
We see the world through a certain lens, it
fits together with our experiences, so we

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.840
think we’re making sense.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:18.310
We think it’s brilliant in terms of our
life experience.

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:21.400
But how do we really know or maybe we won’t?

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:26.570
CSUN Professor Eric Edson: I don’t think
you should know you are one in the class who

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:31.580
are really good because that’s kind of putting
a cap on yourself.

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:37.140
I would say…and we do talk about this (I
point out to them) in terms of (as we’re

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:42.850
workshopping everybody’s work and yes everybody
is at different levels, that I say we all

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:49.460
come to this room from different places we
all have been writing for different periods

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:51.649
of time.

00:00:51.649 --> 00:00:57.010
Some are closer to the beginning than others,
some have already done some stuff, sold some

00:00:57.010 --> 00:01:03.920
stuff, so we are making allowances for that,
that nobody will be on the same level and

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:10.539
I would say that…I would just say don’t
worry about your level.

00:01:10.539 --> 00:01:16.250
It’s not relevant to the process of learning
to master a craft.

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:22.600
And you know, a difficult craft at that.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:24.539
Just do the work in front of you.

00:01:24.539 --> 00:01:28.899
Be you and write what you have to write.

00:01:28.899 --> 00:01:35.700
Because the thing ultimately with writing
and the beauty of it is even when a story

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:40.810
is derivative, perhaps you’ve got an idea
for a plot but you’re saying “No, no,

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:46.350
no…I’ve seen that a score of times before
or through the decades kind of stuff.”

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:53.390
And I would say “Yes, but no one can write
it exactly the way you would write it.”

00:01:53.390 --> 00:02:03.630
It’s not about level, it’s about individual
point of view and insight into the human condition.

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:09.910
And that I would say for all times is to be
encouraged.

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:17.470
That’s what we do, we seek ourselves in
what we write, even when we’re writing for

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:20.610
money (for pay).

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:28.040
And you can overdo that, but I think you need
to be doing it some of that in absolutely

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:32.800
everything you write because, what was that?

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:34.030
Some book came out in the 1930’s.

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:42.260
I forget who wrote it who said there are basically
36 plots in all of literature.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:43.650
That’s it.

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:50.750
Well, that’s what the thing is with genre,
you know with genre are you going to write

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:51.750
a western?

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:56.300
Well that’s been done a few hundred, a few
thousand times, hasn’t it?

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:58.390
Well, you will do it your way.

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:02.730
You will do it the way in which it has not
been done before.

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:09.700
Or if that’s not how it turns out, keep
working on it if you wish or put it in the

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:10.700
drawer.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:17.130
And you will have learned some lessons about
writing and yourself along the way.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:27.230
But the level thing, it’s just that we’re
running different races so much levels.

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:32.770
It’s like some people started sooner than
other people so of course they are going to

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:35.720
be ahead.

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:46.060
But I would admonish writers (neophytes and
experienced ones), don’t worry about that.

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:51.810
You can make yourself nuts worrying about
the level because you will always be writing

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:56.520
what you want to write unless you get hired
to do it for a job.

00:03:56.520 --> 00:04:01.740
But you will be writing what you want to write,
the way you want to write it.

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:08.240
Now just work to make it the best you can
make it be, that’s all.

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:12.620
And one day you may surprise yourself.

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:15.590
Just when you think you aren’t so good and
this happens.

00:04:15.590 --> 00:04:17.400
Oh, we all go in cycles.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:19.040
Yeah, this should be mentioned, too.

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:24.120
I mean up one day and down the next day upset
beyond belief, I mean this is art.

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:25.120
This is writers.

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:26.590
You know, welcome to the club.

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:32.980
On that big wheel, the emotional journey of
what it is, what we do.

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:39.340
But you are also learning whether this art
form is for you or not along the way.

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:40.840
Are you in it for the long haul.

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:44.330
That’s the only question you need to keep
asking yourself.

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:50.370
Am I getting enough food out of this?

00:04:50.370 --> 00:05:00.040
Creative food, juice, and sense of that growing
sense of command (incremental command) of

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:08.490
a much to be respected craft that can be quite
intricate.

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:12.340
That I’m hooked, that this is what I need.

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:19.190
I mean it has been said that you know for
writers, it hurts more not to do it than to

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:21.320
do it.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:27.180
Are you up for a lifetime of all the range
of emotional you are going to be going through

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:29.600
as a writer, as an artist.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:32.750
Is this what you want to do, really?

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:35.470
You want to be an artist, that’s great!

00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:44.770
But understand that it is not the simple and
easy choice to make in life quite the contrary.

00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:51.170
But it is a fabulous, fabulous journey unlike
any other, I think.

